Run host regressions from the repository root:

    python3 test/run_native.py

Requires g++ (or CXX). Tests exercise the real logger and USB adapter with fake
clock, USB FIFO, and mutex implementations. AddressSanitizer and
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer errors fail the run. CI runs these tests after
building both firmware targets.

Coverage includes bounded diagnostic logging with a disconnected or stalled
USB host, a busy USB mutex, partial writes, ring wraparound, full queues,
reentrant callers, message truncation, and rate limiting across clock rollover.

Serial latency retest:
1. Capture USB Serial during normal control traffic and verify the periodic
   summaries and connection events arrive without per-packet logging.
2. Leave the serial port open while pausing host reads long enough for USB
   buffers to fill. Confirm motor commands remain responsive and the watchdog
   disables outputs when control traffic stops.
3. Resume reading and check log_drop/log_supp counters. Repeat with USB
   unplugged.
